  idn("What do you call the activity that helps children learn, explore, develop skills, express feelings, and interact with others?", ["play"], "Play is an activity that helps children learn, explore, develop skills, express feelings, and interact with others.", "Play");
  en("Enumerate the 5 functions of play.", [["Educational", "educat"], ["Recreational", "recreat"], ["Physical development", "physical"], ["Social and emotional", "social", "emotional"], ["Therapeutic", "therapeutic", "therapy"]], "Functions of play: educational, recreational, physical development, social and emotional, therapeutic.");
  mc("Which function of play helps children cope with stress, fear, anxiety and painful experiences?", "Therapeutic", ["Educational", "Recreational", "Physical development"], "Therapeutic - helps children cope with stress, fear, anxiety and painful experiences.");
  en("Enumerate the 7 types of play.", [["Solitary play", "solitary"], ["Onlooker play", "onlooker"], ["Parallel play", "parallel"], ["Associative play", "associative"], ["Cooperative play", "cooperative"], ["Unoccupied play", "unoccupied"], ["Independent play", "independent"]], "Types of play: solitary, onlooker, parallel, associative, cooperative, unoccupied, independent.");
  idn("What type of play is predominant in infants?", ["solitary play", "solitary"], "Solitary play - infant.", "Solitary play");
  idn("What type of play is predominant in toddlers?", ["parallel play", "parallel"], "Parallel play - toddlers: the child plays alongside other children but not with them.", "Parallel play");
  idn("What type of play is predominant in preschoolers?", ["associative play", "associative"], "Associative play - preschoolers: children play together and share toys, but there is no organized goal.", "Associative play");
  idn("What type of play is predominant in school-age children?", ["cooperative play", "cooperative"], "Cooperative play - school-age children: they play together with rules, shared goals and assigned roles.", "Cooperative play");
  mc("In ____ play, the child watches other children play but does not join them.", "Onlooker", ["Solitary", "Cooperative", "Associative"], "Onlooker play - the child watches other children play but does not join them.");
  mc("In ____ play, a child makes random movements and explores the surroundings.", "Unoccupied", ["Independent", "Cooperative", "Onlooker"], "Unoccupied play - a child makes random movements and explores the surroundings.");
  mc("In ____ play, children engage in activities independently, according to their abilities and interests.", "Independent", ["Unoccupied", "Cooperative", "Associative"], "Independent play - children engage in activities independently, according to their abilities and interests.");
  en("Enumerate the 3 criteria for judging the suitability of toys.", [["Safety", "safe"], ["Compatibility", "compatib"], ["Usefulness", "useful"]], "Criteria: safety; compatibility (child's age, level of development, experience); usefulness.");
  mc("How is play important in Maternal and Child Nursing?", "It reduces fear and anxiety during hospitalization", ["It replaces medical treatment", "It increases fear of procedures", "It prevents communication"], "Importance of play in MCN: reduces fear and anxiety during hospitalization; helps children understand procedures through play; etc.");
  mc("How does play help the nurse?", "It helps nurses assess a child's developmental level", ["It lets the nurse skip assessment", "It replaces the parents", "It only keeps the child busy"], "Play helps nurses assess a child's developmental level.");

  pg = "p.9";
  en("Enumerate the 3 dangers to consider about toys during toddlerhood.", [["Breaking a toy through exploration and ingesting small pieces", "break", "small piece", "ingest", "swallow", "choke"], ["Ingesting lead from lead-based paint on toys", "lead", "paint"], ["Being burned by potentially flammable toys", "flammable", "burn"]], "Danger of: breaking a toy through exploration and ingesting small pieces; ingesting lead from lead-based paint; being burned by potentially flammable toys.");
  mc("Imitation and make-believe play begins by ____.", "The end of the second year", ["6 months", "The first birthday", "The sixth year"], "Imitation and make-believe play begins by the end of the second year.");
  mc("Which are suggested toys for toddlers?", "Play furniture, dishes, cooking utensils, telephone, puzzles with a few large pieces", ["Chess and dart games", "Archery and science toys", "Model kits and magic sets"], "Toddlers: play furniture, dishes, cooking utensils, telephone; puzzles with a few large pieces; pedal-propelled toys; clay, sandbox toys, crayons, finger paints; pounding toys, blocks, push-pull toys.");
  mc("In preschool play, the child expresses emotions more through ____.", "Action than through words", ["Words than through action", "Silence", "Reading"], "Through play, the child deals with reality, learns control of feelings, and expresses emotions more through action than through words.");
  mc("Why do school-age children like games with rules?", "Because of increased mental abilities", ["Because of increased motor ability", "Because they cannot play alone", "Because they fear competition"], "Likes games with rules because of increased mental abilities; likes athletic competition because of increased motor ability.");
  mc("In the beginning of school years, boys and girls play together but gradually separate into ____.", "Sex-oriented types of activities", ["Solitary play", "Parallel play", "Unoccupied play"], "Boys and girls play together but gradually separate into sex-oriented types of activities.");
  mc("Which is a suggested play activity for 6 to 9 year olds?", "Physically active games such as hopscotch, jump rope, climbing trees and bicycle riding", ["Archery, dart games and chess", "Pounding toys and push-pull toys", "Rocking horse and straddle toys"], "Suggested play for 6 to 9: housekeeping toys, number games, physically active games (hopscotch, jump rope, climbing trees, bicycle riding), collections and hobbies.");
  mc("Which is a suggested play activity for 9 to 12 year olds?", "Handicrafts, model kits, pottery clay, archery, dart games, chess, jigsaw puzzles, science toys, magic sets", ["Push-pull toys and pounding toys", "Dress-up clothes and puppets", "Rocking horse and finger paints"], "Suggested play for 9 to 12: handicrafts, model kits, pottery clay, hobbies, collections; archery, dart games, chess, jigsaw puzzles; science toys, magic sets.");

  /* ===================== PAIN ASSESSMENT ===================== */
  topic = "Pain Assessment";
  pg = "p.11";
  mc("Which age group shows generalized restlessness, guards or rubs the painful area, and tries to delay painful situations?", "Toddler", ["Preschooler", "School-age", "Adolescent"], "Toddler: generalized restlessness; guards or rubs painful area; loud crying; tries to delay painful situations.");
  idn("What words does a toddler use to describe pain? (Give any one)", ["booboo", "boo boo", "ouch"], "Toddlers use words to describe pain (e.g., BooBoo, ouch).", "BooBoo, ouch");
  mc("A preschooler may believe that pain is ____.", "Punishment for bad behavior", ["A reward", "A normal part of play", "Caused only by germs"], "Preschooler: may believe pain is punishment for bad behavior.");
  mc("Which is a pain response of a preschooler?", "May hit or kick the caregiver", ["Stiff body posture only", "Perceives pain at physical, emotional and mental levels", "Describes intensity of pain exactly"], "Preschooler: crying, can describe pain location; regression; may believe pain is punishment; may deny pain; may hit or kick caregiver.");
  mc("Which age group is afraid of bodily harm and may delay or bargain to avoid painful situations?", "School-age", ["Toddler", "Preschooler", "Infant"], "School-age: stiff body posture; withdrawal; able to describe pain; afraid of bodily harm; may delay or bargain.");
  mc("Which age group recognizes that death exists, as shown in pain assessment?", "School-age", ["Toddler", "Preschooler", "None of the age groups"], "School age: recognizes that death exists.");
  mc("Which age group shows increased muscle tension, decreased activity and withdrawal when in pain?", "Adolescent", ["Toddler", "Preschooler", "School-age"], "Adolescent: increased muscle tension; decreased activity; withdrawal; describes location and intensity of pain.");
  mc("An adolescent perceives pain at which levels?", "Physical, emotional and mental", ["Physical only", "Not at all", "Only when told by parents"], "Adolescent perceives pain at physical, emotional, and mental levels.");

  /* ===================== SITUATIONAL (scenario-based) ===================== */
  const sit = (q, a, w, e) => Q.push({ type: "sit", topic, page: pg, q, a, w, e });

  topic = "Toddler"; pg = "p.2";
  sit("A mother complains that her 2-year-old says \"no\" to everything except candies. How should the nurse explain this behavior?", "It is not abnormal; negativism is a positive change as the toddler establishes identity as a separate individual", ["It is a sign of mental illness that needs treatment", "It shows the child is spoiled and must be strictly punished", "It means the child has not developed object permanence"], "Negativism: toddlers establish identities as separate individuals by saying no all the time. This is not an abnormal phenomenon but a positive change in development.");
  sit("A 2-year-old screams and throws himself on the floor when he cannot tell his mother what he wants. Why do temper tantrums occur at this age?", "Toddlers do not have enough vocabulary to express their feelings in a more acceptable way", ["Toddlers want to punish their parents", "Toddlers have already mastered language", "Toddlers have an overly developed sense of guilt"], "Temper tantrums occur because toddlers do not have enough vocabulary to express their feelings in a more acceptable way.");
  pg = "p.1-2";
  sit("A 20-month-old will eat only when she uses her own spoon. The mother asks if this is normal. The nurse identifies this behavior as ____.", "Ritualistic behavior, which helps the toddler master skills and decrease anxiety", ["Negativism that must be punished", "A sign of poor appetite", "Regression to infancy"], "Ritualistic behavior (e.g., using only their own spoon): the toddler repeats skills to master them and to decrease anxiety.");
  pg = "p.1";
  sit("A toddler will not sleep or go anywhere without her blanket. The nurse recognizes this as a ____.", "Transitional object, a dependency that can normally develop in toddlers", ["Sign of poor parenting", "Sign of a feeding problem", "Habit that must be stopped right away"], "A toddler may develop dependency on a \"transitional object\" such as a blanket or stuffed animal.");
  pg = "p.2";
  sit("A toddler is admitted to the hospital. When his mother leaves, he screams, cries and tries to call her back. Which stage of separation anxiety is this?", "Protest", ["Despair", "Denial", "Autonomy"], "PROTEST: screams and cries when mother leaves, attempts to call her back.");
  sit("After a few days in the hospital, the toddler whimpers, clutches his stuffed toy, curls up in bed and is less active. Which stage of separation anxiety is this?", "Despair", ["Protest", "Denial", "Initiative"], "DESPAIR: whimpers, clutches transitional objects, curls up in bed, decreases activity, rocking.");
  sit("A hospitalized toddler resumes normal activity but ignores his mother when she visits and does not form relationships. Which stage of separation anxiety is this?", "Denial", ["Protest", "Despair", "Guilt"], "DENIAL: resumes normal activity but does not form psychosocial relationships when mother returns; child ignores her.");
  sit("A mother asks when her toddler is ready for toilet training. Which statement by the nurse is correct?", "The child needs control of the rectal and urethral sphincter (usually when walking well), an understanding of holding urine and stools, and a desire to delay gratification", ["Training should start only after the child enters school", "Training can start as soon as the child can sit", "Readiness depends only on the child's weight"], "Toilet training readiness: sphincter control (usually achieved by the time they walk well), cognitive understanding, and a desire to delay immediate gratification.");
  sit("A mother lets her 2-year-old walk around with a lollipop in his mouth and gives him large chunks of hotdog. What should the nurse teach?", "Do not let the child walk around with objects such as lollipops in the mouth, and avoid large chunks of meat such as hotdogs to prevent choking", ["Hotdogs are safe if served cold", "Lollipops are safe as long as the child is happy", "Choking is only a risk for infants"], "Safety: avoid large chunks of meat, particularly hotdogs; do not allow the child to walk around with objects such as lollipops in the mouth.");
  sit("A mother has an 18-month-old who weighs 22 lb. Where and how should the child ride in the car?", "In a forward-facing car seat placed in the rear seat", ["In the front passenger seat, in front of the air bag", "On the mother's lap in the rear seat", "In a booster seat in the front seat"], "Forward-facing seats only after age greater than 1 year and weight greater than 20 lb. All car seats are placed in the rear seat, never in front of the passenger air bag.");
  pg = "p.1";
  sit("A mother is worried because her 2-year-old eats less than before. What should the nurse explain?", "Appetite decreases in toddlers, but the child still needs about 16-24 oz of milk a day", ["It signals a serious illness", "Toddlers need more calories than infants so appetite should increase", "Toddlers should drink 50 oz of milk a day"], "Toddler nutrition: appetite decreases; needs 16-24 oz milk/day; increased need for calcium, iron and phosphorus.");

  topic = "Play"; pg = "p.8";
  sit("A toddler plays beside other children with similar toys but does not interact with them. This is ____.", "Parallel play", ["Associative play", "Cooperative play", "Onlooker play"], "Parallel play - toddlers: the child plays alongside other children but not with them.");
  pg = "p.9";
  sit("The nurse recommends toys for a toddler's increased locomotive skills. Which should she choose?", "Push toys, a rocking horse or a tricycle", ["Chess set and dart games", "Model kits", "Science toys and magic sets"], "Provide toys appropriate for increased locomotive skills: push toys, rocking horse, riding toys or tricycles; swing and slide.");

  topic = "Preschool"; pg = "p.3";
  sit("Which skill would the nurse expect from a healthy 4-year-old?", "Hops on one foot", ["Ties shoes", "Skips and hops on alternate feet", "Jumps rope"], "By 4 years: hops on 1 foot. Skipping, tying shoes and jumping rope are expected by 5 years.");
  pg = "p.4";
  sit("A 4-year-old girl says she wants to marry her father and competes with her mother for his attention. This is ____.", "Electra complex", ["Oedipus complex", "Negativism", "Ritualistic behavior"], "Electra complex - the attachment of a preschool girl to her father (\"daddy's girl\").");
  sit("A 4-year-old boy clings to his mother and competes with his father for her attention. This is ____.", "Oedipus complex", ["Electra complex", "Object permanence", "Egocentrism"], "Oedipus complex - the strong emotional attachment of a preschool boy toward his mother (\"mama's boy\").");
  sit("A preschooler is afraid of the dark and ghosts. Which approach is supported by the notes?", "Expose the child to the feared object in a safe situation to provide a degree of conditioning", ["Tell the child that ghosts will get him if he misbehaves", "Ignore the fear completely", "Force the child to stay alone in the dark"], "Exposing a child to a feared object in a safe situation may provide a degree of conditioning.");
  pg = "p.3";
  sit("A 4-year-old talks and plays with a friend that no one else can see. The mother is worried. What should the nurse say?", "Imaginary playmates are common during the preschool period", ["It is a sign of severe mental illness", "The child should be punished", "It only occurs in school-age children"], "Imaginary playmates are common during this period.");
  pg = "p.4";
  sit("A 4-year-old boy stutters and his mother asks about it. What is the best explanation?", "It results from failure to master sensorimotor integration, affects boys more often than girls, and resolves during childhood", ["It is caused by the mother's lack of attention", "It is permanent and cannot resolve", "It affects girls more often than boys"], "Speech problem: failure to master sensorimotor integration results in stuttering or stammering; it affects boys more frequently than girls and resolves during childhood.");
  sit("A mother is alarmed that her preschooler touches his genitalia. What should the nurse explain?", "It is part of sexual curiosity and exploration", ["It is always a sign of sexual abuse", "It is a sign of a severe psychiatric disorder", "It only happens in adolescents"], "Masturbation or self-stimulation of the genitalia is part of sexual curiosity and exploration.");
  pg = "p.3";
  sit("A 4-year-old weighs 45 lb. What is the correct car restraint for this child?", "Booster seat", ["Rear-facing infant seat", "Adult seat belt only", "Front passenger seat"], "Children over 40 lb and between ages 4 and 8 should have a booster seat.");
  sit("A preschool boy and girl love dressing up and using a doctor and nurse's kit. Which statement is correct?", "Preschoolers enjoy imitative and dramatic play and imitate same-sex role functions", ["This shows a developmental delay", "Preschoolers should be limited to solitary play", "This type of play is only for school-age children"], "Enjoys imitative and dramatic play: imitates same-sex role functions; enjoys dressing up, dollhouses, doctor and nurse's kit.");

  topic = "School-Age"; pg = "p.5";
  sit("An 8-year-old falls from his bike and fractures his arm. Why are school-age children prone to fractures?", "Bone growth is faster than muscle and ligament development", ["Their bones have stopped growing", "Their vision is not yet mature", "Their gross motor skills are poor"], "Bone growth is faster than muscle and ligament development - children are very limber but susceptible to bone fractures.");
  sit("A 7-year-old believes that things are either right or wrong and that rules must never be broken. This is ____.", "Moral realism", ["Autonomous morality", "Egocentrism", "Decentering"], "Before age 9, moral realism predominates: strict superego, rule dominance, things are black or white.");
  sit("A 10-year-old understands that people have different points of view and sees \"gray\" areas. This is ____.", "Autonomous morality", ["Moral realism", "Magical thinking", "Object permanence"], "After age 9, autonomous morality develops: recognizes differing points of view and sees \"gray\" areas.");
  sit("A child pours juice from a tall narrow glass into a wide glass and says the amount is still the same. This shows ____.", "Conservation", ["Class inclusion", "Decentering", "Magical thinking"], "Conservation - the ability to appreciate that a change in shape does not necessarily mean a change in quantity.");
  sit("A child understands that a dog can be both a pet and an animal. This shows ____.", "Class inclusion", ["Conservation", "Object permanence", "Magical thinking"], "Class inclusion - the ability to understand that objects can belong to more than one classification.");
  sit("A 9-year-old imagines how his friend feels and looks at the situation from his friend's viewpoint instead of only his own. This is ____.", "Decentering", ["Conservation", "Class inclusion", "Egocentrism"], "Decentering - the ability to project one's self into other people's situations and see the world from their viewpoint.");
  pg = "p.6";
  sit("A 9-year-old often refuses to go to school and complains of stomach pain every morning, but no physical cause is found. What may be happening?", "School phobia resulting in psychosomatic illness", ["Normal growth change", "Mature vision development", "Autonomous morality"], "Fears of school-age children: school phobia may develop, resulting in psychosomatic illness.");
  sit("A school-age child eats chips, soda and candies daily and is gaining excessive weight. What should the nurse emphasize?", "Junk food (excess sugar, starches and fat) puts the child at risk for obesity, and nutrition education should be part of the school program", ["Junk food is recommended for energy", "Obesity is not a risk in this age group", "Only toddlers need nutrition education"], "\"Junk food\" may become a problem; obesity is at risk; nutrition education should be integrated in the school program.");
  sit("A 10-year-old wants to join a team, follow the rules and be accepted by his peers. Which statement is correct?", "Rules and rituals dominate play; knowing rules provides a sense of belonging, and team play teaches the nature of competition", ["Individuality is strongly encouraged by peers", "School-age children prefer only parallel play", "Team games have no developmental value"], "Rules and ritual dominate play; individuality is not tolerated by peers; team play helps learn the value of team accomplishment and the nature of competition.");

  topic = "Adolescent"; pg = "p.7";
  sit("A 15-year-old wants freedom but complains about the responsibilities that come with it and wishes for her carefree childhood. This is ____.", "Ambivalence", ["Negativism", "Egocentrism", "Conservation"], "Ambivalence: the adolescent wants freedom but is not happy about corresponding responsibilities.");
  sit("A 16-year-old insists on dressing and acting just like her group of friends. Which concept explains this?", "Peer-group identity, one of the strongest motivating forces of behavior", ["Egocentrism of the preschooler", "Ritualistic behavior", "Object permanence"], "Peer-group identity is one of the strongest motivating forces of behavior; it is extremely important to be part of the group and like everyone else.");
  sit("A 15-year-old understands sarcasm and jokes with double meanings. Which cognitive stage is she in?", "Formal operational thought", ["Magical thinking", "Moral realism", "Object permanence"], "Formal operational thought: abstract thinking; can comprehend satire and double meanings.");
  sit("An 11-year-old girl grows taller and gains weight rapidly. Her mother asks if this is normal. What should the nurse say?", "Yes, the pubertal growth spurt in females occurs between 10 and 14 years", ["No, growth spurts occur only after 17 years", "No, growth spurts occur only in males", "Yes, but only after menopause"], "Females: pubertal growth spurt between 10 and 14.");
  sit("The nurse plans a health talk for adolescents about concerns regarding sexuality and sexual activity. Which topics belong in the talk?", "Unplanned pregnancies, STIs and stalking", ["Toilet training, ritualistic behavior and tantrums", "Separation anxiety and object permanence", "Stuttering and imaginary playmates"], "Concerns regarding sexuality and sexual activity: unplanned pregnancies, STIs (Sexually Transmitted Infections), stalking.");

